members.description:
`getTitle` is used to draw titles outside the [`RadarChart`](https://pub.dev/documentation/fl_chart/latest/fl_chart/RadarChart-class.html)
`getTitle` is type of [`GetTitleByIndexFunction`](https://pub.dev/documentation/fl_chart/latest/fl_chart/GetTitleByIndexFunction.html) so you should return a valid [`RadarChartTitle`](#radarcharttitle)
for each `index` (we provide a default `angle` = index * 360 / titleCount)

```dart
getTitle: (index, angle) {
  switch (index) {
    case 0:
      return RadarChartTitle(text: 'Mobile or Tablet', angle: angle);
    case 2:
      return RadarChartTitle(text: 'Desktop', angle: angle);
    case 1:
      return RadarChartTitle(text: 'TV', angle: angle);
    default:
      return const RadarChartTitle(text: '');
  }
}
```

the `titlePositionPercentageOffset` is the place of showing title on the [`RadarChart`](https://pub.dev/documentation/fl_chart/latest/fl_chart/RadarChart-class.html)
The higher the value of this field, the more titles move away from the chart.
this field should be between 0 and 1,
if it is 0 the title will be drawn near the inside section,
if it is 1 the title will be drawn near the outside of section,
the default value is 0.2.
